{
 "form_8k_item_401": {
  "company": "Halloran Bay Packaging, Inc.",
  "filed": "2026-09-18",
  "paragraphs": [
   "On September 14, 2026, Pemberton Rhodes LLP ('Pemberton') informed the Audit Committee of the Board of Directors of Halloran Bay Packaging, Inc. (the 'Company') that it declined to stand for re-appointment as the Company's independent registered public accounting firm for the fiscal year ending December 31, 2026. Pemberton will continue to serve until the completion of its review of the Company's interim financial statements for the quarter ending September 30, 2026.",
   "Pemberton's reports on the Company's consolidated financial statements for the fiscal years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 did not contain an adverse opinion or a disclaimer of opinion, and were not qualified or modified as to uncertainty, audit scope or accounting principles.",
   "During the fiscal years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 and the subsequent interim period through September 14, 2026, there were no disagreements (as defined in Item 304(a)(1)(iv) of Regulation S-K) with Pemberton on any matter of accounting principles or practices, financial statement disclosure, or auditing scope or procedure, and there were no reportable events (as defined in Item 304(a)(1)(v) of Regulation S-K).",
   "The Audit Committee has begun a process to select a new independent registered public accounting firm and expects to complete it before the end of the fourth quarter of 2026.",
   "The Company provided Pemberton with a copy of the disclosures in this Item 4.01 and requested that Pemberton furnish a letter addressed to the Securities and Exchange Commission stating whether it agrees with the statements made by the Company. Pemberton's letter is filed as Exhibit 16.1."
  ]
 },
 "exhibit_16_1": {
  "date": "2026-09-18",
  "from": "Pemberton Rhodes LLP, Hartford, Connecticut",
  "to": "Securities and Exchange Commission, Office of the Chief Accountant",
  "text": "We have read Item 4.01 of Halloran Bay Packaging, Inc.'s Form 8-K dated September 18, 2026, and have the following comments: (1) We agree with the statements made in the first, second and fifth paragraphs. (2) We agree with the statement in the third paragraph that there were no disagreements. We do not agree with the statement in the third paragraph that there were no reportable events. On August 27, 2026, we informed the Audit Committee that information had come to our attention concerning the timing of revenue recognized on bill-and-hold arrangements with two customers during the quarters ended March 31, 2026 and June 30, 2026 which, if further investigated, may materially impact the fairness or reliability of the Company's interim financial statements for those quarters, and that the scope of our procedures would need to be expanded. As of the date of this letter, that investigation has not been completed. (3) We have no basis to agree or disagree with the statements made in the fourth paragraph."
 },
